````markdown
# FileMate — Full-Stack Agentic App with Guardrails

An AI assistant that turns receipt text into filed expense reports against a **mock**
Expense API. The point of the app is the controls, not the chat: a human approves
every write, guardrails run in code, and every run is logged with a trace ID.

- **Frontend:** React + Vite (`frontend/`)
- **Backend:** FastAPI + LangGraph agent, OpenAI `gpt-4o-mini` (`backend/`)
- **Signed-in user:** Priya Nair, `E1042` (taken from the session, never the message)

## Architecture sketch

```
React UI (:5173)
  │  POST /chat, /actions/{id}/approve|reject|edit, GET /runs      (never calls the LLM or Expense API directly)
  ▼
FastAPI backend (:8000)  app/main.py
  ├─ input + scope guardrails ───────── app/guardrails.py   (before the LLM)
  ├─ LangGraph agent (3 read + 3 write tools) ─ app/agent.py + app/tools.py
  │     reads → mock API now;  writes → STAGED, never executed here
  ├─ HITL pending-action store (hash-bound) ─ app/hitl.py
  ├─ approved payload executor ──────── app/executor.py     (only path to a real write)
  ├─ in-memory mock Expense API ─────── app/mock_expense_api.py (seed data + policy)
  └─ structured JSON logging + /runs ── app/observability.py (one trace ID per run)
```

Read tools go straight to the API. Every write stops at the pending-action store;
only an approval runs the stored payload. Edit creates a new pending action; Reject
hands control back to the agent.

## How to run (one command)

```bash
cd filemate
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-... ./run.sh
```

This boots the backend on `http://localhost:8000` (creating its venv on first run)
and the UI on `http://localhost:5173`. Open the UI and paste a receipt such as
`Uber trip, Airport to office, 1250 INR, 28 Oct 2026, project ATLAS`.

Run the tests and regenerate the log sample:

```bash
cd backend && ./.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q
./.venv/bin/python scripts/make_log_sample.py        # writes logs/sample_run.jsonl (D4)
```

## Where each control lives in the code

| Control | File | What enforces it |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Input checks (length/empty/text) | `app/guardrails.py` `check_input` | called in `main.py chat()` **before** the LLM |
| Employee ID from session | `app/config.py SESSION_EMPLOYEE_ID`; `app/agent.py` prompt | `ChatRequest` has no employee field; tools use the session ID |
| Tool-argument checks | `app/guardrails.py` `validate_line_args` | run in `tools.py add_expense_line` **before** staging |
| Typed extraction schema | `app/schemas.py` `ExpenseLine` | `tools.py add_expense_line` coerces the model's args into `ExpenseLine` before anything else |
| Policy / justification | `app/guardrails.py` `policy_check` | over-limit sets `needs_justification`; `hitl.py approve` refuses until set |
| Valid write sequence | `app/main.py` `_assemble_write_payload` | the payload is assembled as create → line(s) → submit, not trusted from tool-call order |
| Prompt injection | `app/guardrails.py` `detect_injection` | logged in `main.py`; receipt wrapped as data in `agent.py` |
| Scope / authorization | `app/guardrails.py` `check_scope` / `check_read_scope` | refuses off-topic and other-employee requests |
| **HITL gate (the key line)** | `app/hitl.py HitlStore.approve` | status + payload-hash check; **writes only happen in `executor.py`, reached only from `approve`** |
| Output check ("filed") | `app/main.py approve()` / `executor.py` | the success message is built from the real API result, not the model |
| Observability | `app/observability.py` | one JSON line per event, shared `trace_id`, masked args, `GET /runs` |

The single line that stops a write without approval: `HitlStore.approve` raises unless
the action is `pending`, needs no justification, and still matches its stored hash;
nothing else calls `executor.execute`.

